@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}

The changes look INCREDIBLY stuffed and claustrophobic despite there being less buttons now.

I honestly feel less inclined to be in the avatar menu now.

As a professional ui/ux designer of eight years, Here's how you fix it;

Rollback the original avatar menu.

Move the new Avatar Market component to the Marketplace tab, where it should've been to start with, for a consistent and intuitive storefront.

Specific feedback;

The new avatar menu pane design fails basic ux design on several counts;

It's inconsistent with the rest of the client app.

It prioritizes browsing, and assigns the largest button to Details over Applying an avatar for a purchase-focused layout and makes it harder to apply avatars because it's a secondary button.  This is bad design when the primary use-case should ALWAYS be the user applying owned avatars.

The tick doesn't infer what it does at a glance vs "Apply".  Position should also  be swapped with the Details button, which can be inferred by using the avatar quality icons instead of text for visual shorthand of the details tab and the avatar's rating itself.

None of these changes should require major code changes that may break a build, only moving existing component placement in the UI layout and icon change on existing buttons.

